```sql
--Description:  Because the tables were created with un-quoted column names, Snowflake stores
--              them internally in uppercase.  Referencing a quoted, lowercase name like
--              "geo_id" therefore fails.  Below, the identifiers are left un-quoted so they
--              resolve correctly.  The query joins the 2015 and 2018 ZIP-code ACS 5-year
--              tables on geo_id, computes the change in median_household_income, filters to
--              ZIP codes where income fell (income_diff < 0), and returns 20 illustrative rows.
SELECT
       a.geo_id                               AS geo_id,
       a.median_household_income              AS income_2015,
       b.median_household_income              AS income_2018,
       b.median_household_income - a.median_household_income AS income_diff
FROM   CENSUS_BUREAU_ACS_2.CENSUS_BUREAU_ACS.ZIP_CODES_2015_5YR a
JOIN   CENSUS_BUREAU_ACS_2.CENSUS_BUREAU_ACS.ZIP_CODES_2018_5YR b
       ON a.geo_id = b.geo_id
WHERE  b.median_household_income - a.median_household_income < 0
LIMIT 20;
```
